Fresh proofs produced `#Top` and were non-vacuous, but the generated semantics models UTF-8 byte offsets instead of Python character indices. For `"😀A😀E"`, both Python implementations return `0`, while the proved K program returns `1`. It also omits reachable `RecursionError` behavior on long strings.

Detailed seven-stage report: [REVIEW.md](/audit-output/REVIEW.md)  
Preserved evidence: [evidence](/audit-output/evidence/)
